h-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"ae468f391045fa9c79c18bed34e24e9de09dc30df4ca699e57286741ee1f7062","event_uuid":"45a125b3-5a40-4567-b6d7-acb55160bf68","position":{"commit_sha":"4bfcc257ff6d0337a5cbbe367c7e725c187831cd","position":"1786995443206927001-45a125b3-5a40-4567-b6d7-acb55160bf68"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"c64c1a9e5e0b1cf4e9753b4efa6967d06945a5f7d635864e7d5e09510dd41859","event_uuid":"f589a7bf-92b4-41e4-adda-b16faebba903","position":{"commit_sha":"2aa8536bb0335a92d25cd5067a428eb9fd95296d","position":"1786995588359030001-f589a7bf-92b4-41e4-adda-b16faebba903"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"b5c478f99b40787431f4f30800303a082baca3b32dc299cc3b0f110d5ba86bbb","event_uuid":"8f9e5421-1470-4540-9bc6-cfb0968a1da0","position":{"commit_sha":"6bf8f9f3e3bb89d199488040117476c4e669ee9d","position":"1786995730820825001-8f9e5421-1470-4540-9bc6-cfb0968a1da0"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1786995167427720001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"1c4d7875-4026-4bc4-9458-9314442c912d","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"e042-4780-6c63-4b09"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\nAfter S2, read/check paths use operation bindings, but live apply, Git push, ACLI/delivery, and bridge orchestration still rebuild config or reuse broad parent environments. Jira Cloud write scope still has the local `DIG` fallback. These paths can write under an unintended scope or leak a Rebar-materialized credential to an unrelated sibling child.\n\n## Outcome\nCut write/apply and subprocess paths over to the S2 runtime. Add one shared child-environment builder: trusted same-capability children start from ambient inheritance, owning children receive their adapter overlay, unrelated siblings remove exact secret names declared by other Rebar adapters, unknown native Git/SSH/AWS/proxy/CA variables survive, and Rebar never mutates global `os.environ`.\n\n## Plan\n1. Thread `ReconcilerSettings`, `GitRuntime`, selected `BridgeRuntime`, and the already-constructed backend through applier, mutation planning/dispatch, inbound/outbound handlers, binding updates, Git adapter/ref/lock/push, and `_bridge_runner` delivery paths. Remove their ambient `load_config`/cwd/default fallbacks.\n2. Add `src/rebar/_child_env.py` with a pure environment projection API and a checked-in registry of exact secret names owned by each Rebar adapter. The registry contains names, never values; native SDK/helper chains remain ambient.\n3. Ensure CLI `-c` tracker/Jira/reconciler selections cross the reconciler subprocess boundary as non-secret snapshot material. Pass static adapter material only to the exact owning process/adapter.\n4. Remove the Jira Cloud write-side `DIG` fallback. Missing explicit write scope fails before mutation. Preserve existing retry, rate-limit, TLS, output, partial-failure, idempotency, and ticket-delivery behavior unless a test names the approved delta.\n\n## Testing (RED -> GREEN)\n- End-to-end verified-fake Cloud/DC runs cover create/update/comment/link/delete/inbound apply plus Git commit/push/delivery under custom tracker dir/branch/remote with ambient resolvers poisoned after composition.\n- Child-process contract tests assert unknown ambient/native-chain variables survive; the owning overlay appears only for its child; unrelated siblings lose other adapters' exact declared names; argv/URL/log/output contain no secret sentinel.\n- Concurrency tests run distinct operations with different overlays and timeouts, asserting `os.environ` is byte-equal before/during/after and no cross-operation value is observed.\n- Failure-injection tests cover missing project/auth, revoked credential, TLS error, retry/rate-limit exhaustion, provider partial failure, and delivery failure; existing provider-neutral output and recovery/idempotency oracles remain authoritative.\n- A red test demonstrates the current `DIG` fallback; green asserts zero provider mutation when write scope is absent.\n\n## Compatibility / rollback\nUntil bounded-live validation, a compatibility facade may invoke the legacy write path. Before cutover, rollback selects it. After any new snapshot-aware caller ships, rollback requires the S1 envelope-compatible floor. Ticket, event, bridge, and binding formats remain unchanged.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Verified-fake Cloud/DC apply plus Git/delivery paths complete with ambient resolvers poisoned and use the configured tracker directory/branch/remote and explicit project scope.\n- [ ] Missing Cloud write scope produces a typed/redacted pre-mutation failure and no request uses `DIG` unless `DIG` was explicitly configured.\n- [ ] Same-capability child tests preserve unknown Git/SSH/AWS/proxy/CA variables, owning children receive only their overlay, and unrelated siblings omit every other adapter's exact declared secret name.\n- [ ] Concurrent-operation tests prove no global environment mutation and no cross-operation credential/config observation.\n- [ ] Existing retry, rate-limit, TLS, output, partial-failure, recovery, and idempotency scenarios retain their provider-neutral behavior except explicitly approved deltas.\n- [ ] Disabling the write facade restores the legacy path before cutover; no stored ticket/event/bridge/binding format changes.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_child_env.py","reason":"Pure adapter-owned child environment projection and exact secret-name registry."},{"path":"src/rebar/_bridge_runner.py","reason":"Pass the operation snapshot/runtime and scope child delivery environments."},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/applier.py","reason":"Use the one selected backend/runtime for apply."},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/apply_base.py","reason":"Thread runtime through common mutation services."},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/apply_handlers.py","reason":"Replace handler ambient config reads with projections."},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/apply_inbound.py","reason":"Use operation runtime for inbound apply."},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/apply_inbound_records.py","reason":"Use injected identity/backend without ambient construction."},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/apply_outbound.py","reason":"Use operation runtime for outbound apply."},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/apply_planning.py","reason":"Carry configured root/layout and policy through write planning."},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/dispatch_one.py","reason":"Thread immutable runtime through single-ticket dispatch."},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/dispatch_apply_phases.py","reason":"Thread immutable runtime through apply phases."},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/git_adapter.py","reason":"Honor configured Git runtime and tracker layout."},{"path":"src/rebar/_store/push.py","reason":"Use scoped child environments for Git push without global mutation."},{"path":"tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/mutate/","reason":"Apply/delta/failure/idempotency and explicit-project oracles."},{"path":"tests/unit/test_child_env.py","reason":"Ambient inheritance, exact sibling removal, owning overlay, and concurrency oracles."},{"path":"tests/interfaces/store/test_reconciler_apply_bindings.py","reason":"Verified-fake Cloud/DC apply plus Git/delivery end-to-end coverage."}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[["depends_on","e042-4780-6c63-4b09"],["parent","e215-ab23-ed6a-4791"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"e215-ab23-ed6a-4791","parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":1,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":["rp04","config","reconciler","security"],"ticket_id":"6e3b-3d1a-0ff7-44b6","ticket_type":"story","title":"RP-04 S3 — Cut reconciler apply and child processes to scoped runtimes","verify_commands":[{"command":"env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" .venv/bin/pytest -q tests/unit/test_child_env.py","dd_id":"AC2-AC4","dd_text":"Child environment ownership and concurrent no-global-mutation contract"},{"command":"env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" .venv/bin/pytest -q tests/interfaces/store/test_reconciler_apply_bindings.py","dd_id":"AC1-AC6","dd_text":"Verified-fake Cloud/DC apply plus Git/delivery end-to-end behavior"},{"command":"env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" .venv/bin/pytest -q tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/mutate","dd_id":"REGRESSION","dd_text":"Existing mutation failure/idempotency and provider output behavior"}]},"source_event_uuids":["15d052ba-de28-45e6-8b3d-20684b08da6e","f0c306df-8b69-4931-b157-7a3c38959410","1c4d7875-4026-4bc4-9458-9314442c912d","45a125b3-5a40-4567-b6d7-acb55160bf68","f589a7bf-92b4-41e4-adda-b16faebba903","8f9e5421-1470-4540-9bc6-cfb0968a1da0"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1786999211819391001,"uuid":"b6e62d3e-3e20-4f34-8235-715bef80229f"}